WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:02.435
 Mark, Scott, congratulations.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.203
You guys have made it to
the third and final round

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.471
of this competition.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.073
Now we're asking you to go
back to your home forges

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.709
and recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.945
[music playing]

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.713
The Dussage.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:15.681
 Ooh.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:16.549
 Yes.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.350
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.119
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:19.919
 Good luck, buddy.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:20.686
 You're the man.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.223 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:25.525
 Here we are.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:26.759
Ready to kill it.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:30.129
I want to have this blade
shaped and ready for heat treat.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.064
If I could heat treat
on the end of day one

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.100
I'll be really good in line.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.302
Right now I am going
to start trying

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.404
to grind a little bit
of paper in this blade

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.340
and make sure that fuller sets
in as deep as I can get it.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:43.443
Kind of thinned it
out a little bit.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.079
I didn't want to grind too
much before heat treat.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.680
That looks rad.

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:49.015
I like that a lot.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.516
Once I got this
thing rubbed to shape

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.352
and got the bend in with
my little whacking method,

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:55.655
it was time to
just heat treat it.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.557
All right, boys and girls.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.193
[music playing]

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.064
Yeah, she's nice and straight.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.265
Oh, yeah.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.167
It's a hard blade, so I
can't stress how happy

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.869
I am actually inside right now.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.439 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.574
 It's day one.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.542
I'm back in Emporia, Kansas,
and I'm making a Dussage.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.577
The plan for day one
is to get the blade

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:21.947
forged out, thermal
cycled, and then hardened.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:23.816
There's a lot put
into the handle work.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.486
So I'm wanting to get my forging
done as quick as possible.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.789
I always like to forge
thick, grind thin,

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:33.193
not have to worry about warps.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.695
One of the hardest parts is
done, getting your tang done.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:39.399
Now just put a point on
it, hammer the bevels in.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.102
[music playing]

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.538
At this point I got
the blade forged out.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.307
[music playing]

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.543
I get it down into the oil.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.745
[music playing]

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.348
Oh yeah, baby, that's a
good sign right there.

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.683
No warp, it's nice and straight.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.918
This is a huge relief.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.519
It's like when you have to poop
and then you finally get to go,

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.289 line:8%
it's just one of the
best feelings ever.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.456 line:14%
 Beginning of day three.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.626 line:8%
I'm feeling spunky,
ready to get going.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:07.727
Let's get to work.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.628
Today is going to be making
that clamshell guard,

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:13.132
so I have chunks of lead
that I use for casting.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.534
And so I'm going
to use that lead.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.802
I think it'll absorb that
steel a little bit better.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:20.573
The first thing to do is make
myself a die with rounded edges

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.340
and round nose.

00:02:21.406 --> 00:02:22.474
I'm just going to smash into it.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:24.577
That's going to turn
out pretty nice.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.346
[music playing]

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.014
I was hitting it with
the ball-peen hammer

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.348
and realized that
I actually like

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.183
the hammer look into this
lead block a lot better,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.819
so I just ran with it.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.454
Dude, that thing's
fitting awesome.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.556
End of day three, got a lot
more done than I anticipated.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:40.326 line:8%
So things are cruising
along pretty good.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.262 line:8%
 Start out on day four and the
last part of the guard I have

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:45.064
to make's the clamshell guard.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.732
So I just laid it out on
a piece of sheet metal,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.503
cut it out, and started
working it from there.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.605
Once I get the lines
put in the clamshell,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.241
I stick it in the forge,
and I actually start curving

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:56.576
it to the shape of my fist.

00:02:59.011 --> 00:02:59.679
Woo!

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:00.980
Damn, that's hot.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:04.350
It's really important you get
it snug enough to actually work

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.385
properly and protect
your fist but also

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.455
it's not so tight that it's
just digging into your hand.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.690
Guard done.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:13.025
Final assembly, that's what
I'm going to be working on now.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.228
[music playing]

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:19.131
It is the end of day four
and I'm feeling great

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:23.302
because I finished my
sword and it looks good.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.570
 Beginning of day four.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.939
All I got to do is make
sure this thing's sharp.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.909
Let's slice some fruit up and
let's see this thing work.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.379
[music playing]

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.281
This thing is razor-sharp.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.416
The sword feels
great for me, so I'm

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.751
hoping it's the
same for somebody

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:39.752
who knows how to use one.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.320
It tastes good, too.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.354
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:45.524
Welcome to the kill test.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:46.826
 To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.427
your weapon will do,
I'll take your weapon

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.096
and I'm going to put
some slashes and thrusts

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.764
on this pig carcass.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:52.765
Scott, you're first.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:53.566
You ready for this?

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.267
 Oh, yeah.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.668
 Let's do this.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:59.171
 I am super excited to see Doug
chop up a pig with my blade.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.573
I run my mouth all
the time like, I

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:01.974
can do that, I can do that.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.911
So now's the time to see if
I can really walk the walk,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.746
because I know I
can talk the talk.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.882
[music playing]

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.691
Ooh.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.794
[music playing]

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.332
 All right, Scott.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.869
First up, it is light.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:33.105
The balance really allows
for velocity and recovery

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.273
with this blade.

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:37.576
And most importantly,
it will kill.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:38.444
 Yeah.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:39.845
 All right, Mark.
Your turn, sir.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:40.679
Are you ready?

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:41.581
 Heck yeah.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:43.515
 Let's do this.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:46.752
 I'm ready to see my
sword destroy, cut, slice.

00:04:46.818 --> 00:04:48.921
But I want to see the
insides of that pig.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:52.658
Oh.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.295
[music playing]

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.844
 It's just hanging
there like chewing gum.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:12.645
 All right, Mark.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:13.880
Let's talk about
your blade here.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.115
It's beautiful in its creation.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:17.583
The edge is sharp.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.118
I was quite amazed
with the cuts.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.287
I was surprised that
it cut that deeply.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.890
The one thing, though,
is that that guard right

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.657
there, that rubs on my knuckle.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.126
Not bad, but it does
rub on the knuckle.

00:05:28.193 --> 00:05:30.129
Despite that, it will kill.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:30.863
 Yes.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:34.566
[music playing]

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:35.768
 Hoo.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.669
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:38.036
Welcome to the strength test.

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:40.873
The whiskey barrel chop.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.008
 Yeah.

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:43.542
 Now, to test of the strength
and overall construction

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.244
of your swords, I
will be swinging

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.245
into these whiskey barrels.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.780
So Scott, you're up first.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:48.614
You're ready for this?

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.147
 Oh yeah.

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:50.049
 All right.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:53.419
[music playing]

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:07.166
 Oh.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.834
 First off, Scott,
this thing is

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:12.337
still a razor blade
on its entire length

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:13.705
except for right there.

00:06:13.772 --> 00:06:17.443
You did take a bit of a roll
there and a very small chip.

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:20.179
But beautiful
craftsmanship, super light,

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.781
fast blade, very strong.

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:23.649
Nicely done.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.184
 Thank you.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.084
 Mark you're up next.

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:26.852
You're ready for this?

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:27.653
 Smash them.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.354
 OK.

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:31.023
[music playing]

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.829
 Here she goes.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.532
[music playing]

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:57.349
 All right, Mark.

00:06:57.382 --> 00:06:58.917
Got an edge all the
way across this thing.

00:06:58.984 --> 00:06:59.518
 Yes.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.987
 You didn't lose a bit.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:03.956
The only issue I have with this
weapon at all, as Doug said,

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:08.727
my knuckle rides right there
on the inside of the guard.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:10.763
It's not chewing my
hand up, but there

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:13.932
is contact right there where
I don't necessarily want it.

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:15.033
It's a beautiful weapon.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.068
It's strong.

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:16.835
Nicely done.

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:17.737
 Thank you.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:20.106
[music playing]

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:22.741
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.076
This is the sharpness test.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.644
The four pillar slice.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:29.048
These pillars are wrapped in
different materials-- foam,

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:31.149
leather, canvas, and silk.

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:32.351
Scott, you're up first.

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.085
Ready for this?

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.487
 Oh yeah.

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:36.789
[music playing]

00:07:53.405 --> 00:07:54.506
 All right.

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:55.474
Scott, let's talk
about your weapon here.

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:56.375
It is light.

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:58.610
Every cut it cuts nicely.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:01.980
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:02.948
 Thank you.

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:04.950
 All right, Mark,
onto your shiny sword.

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:05.918
You ready for this?

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:06.919
 Slice and dice.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:10.089
[music playing]

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:34.312
 All right, Mark, let's
talk about your blade here.

00:08:34.379 --> 00:08:35.781
That's a cutter right there.

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:37.950
You can feel the weight and
the power with your slashes

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:38.684
with this.

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.652
On the leather it did cut.

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:42.087
It's just because the
thicker kind of blade

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.090
that you have here it didn't
cut all the way through.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:47.759
But overall sir, it will cut.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:49.061
 Nice.

00:08:49.127 --> 00:08:52.665
 Mark, Scott, both of you
guys turned in incredibly

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.000
competitive blades.

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:57.002
However, the judges have
completed their deliberation,

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.670
they've made their
final decision.

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:04.376
Our new "Forged in
Fire" champion is Scott.

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.912
Congratulations.

00:09:06.978 --> 00:09:10.215
Mark, unfortunately the judges
have decided that your blade

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.517
doesn't make the cut.

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:13.219
 Mark, when we have a
competition with two blades

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:16.154
that perform as amazingly
as your two blades do,

00:09:16.221 --> 00:09:19.125
it comes down to judging the
craftsmanship of the blade.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.026
Your blade rubbed our knuckles.

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:24.029
For that small reason,
we're letting you go.

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:24.964
 Understand.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:28.934
 Mark, please
surrender your blade.

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:31.770 line:8%
 I'm bummed that I lost,
but I'm very proud of myself

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:33.105 line:14%
and what I've accomplished.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:34.273
 That was a fine piece, man.

00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:36.208
 Going home because my
guard was rubbing the judge's

00:09:36.274 --> 00:09:40.212
knuckles just a slight bit,
that little teeny tiny detail,

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:41.514
you live and you learn.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.981
 Mark is an amazing bladesmith.

00:09:43.048 --> 00:09:45.985
If it wasn't for Mark telling
me I could do this, I got this.

00:09:46.018 --> 00:09:46.751
 Good job, buddy.

00:09:46.818 --> 00:09:48.220
 I'd be the one going home.

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:50.756
 I really hope I make
my kids proud with this.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:55.494
And the world gets to see what
Cool Beans Knives gets to do.

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:58.064
[music playing]

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.665
 Well, Scott, in
one of our tightest

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:02.301
competitions to date you've
become the "Forged in Fire"

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.435
champion, and
that's a title that

00:10:03.501 --> 00:10:06.238
comes with a check for $10,000.

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.138
Good job.

00:10:07.205 --> 00:10:08.006
 Thank you.

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:09.274
Ah!

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:10.142
I won, baby!

00:10:10.176 --> 00:10:11.276
Yes!

00:10:11.343 --> 00:10:13.679
This ranks up there with getting
married, having children.

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:17.016
Oh, yeah, I'm a Forged in Fire
champion, too, by the way.

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:18.083
What's next for me?

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.552
Get my 10 grand in ones so
I can roll around in it.

00:10:20.619 --> 00:10:21.653
You know, normal stuff.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.522
You know, what
normal champions do.

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:26.892
[music playing]

